     A* *********************************************************
     A*  IVVRPCWRK
     A*  Work with Repricing Suggestions - display file
     A* *********************************************************
     A*  The screen an editor approves or overrides a suggestion on,
     A*  which is what phase 1 means: AS400 puts up a number and a
     A*  person decides.
     A*
     A*  Two lines per suggestion. The first shows what the price is
     A*  now, what is suggested, when the title is due to re-run and
     A*  when it was last repriced - the four things needed to judge
     A*  the number without leaving the screen. The second shows the
     A*  note: the bracket used, or why the line is held.
     A*
     A*  Options:  2  override, using the price typed in the New column
     A*            4  reject, leaving the price alone
     A*            6  approve the suggested price
     A*
     A*  An override past the catalogue cap is not refused. It is held on
     A*  the file at status 'G' and reported, and typing 2 again on the
     A*  held line authorises it - so the confirmation survives a
     A*  refresh, a sign-off and a shift change, and is recorded against
     A*  the editor who gave it.
     A*
     A*  SCYCL is hidden rather than shown: each line has to carry its own
     A*  key, and the cycle is of no interest to the person reading it.
     A* *********************************************************
     A                                      DSPSIZ(24 80 *DS3)
     A                                      PRINT
     A                                      CA03(03 'Exit')
     A                                      CF05(05 'Refresh')
     A                                      CA12(12 'Cancel')
     A* Subfile record - one repricing suggestion, two lines
     A          R RPCSFL1                   SFL
     A            SOPT           1A  B  7  3VALUES(' ' '2' '4' '6')
     A            SITEM          8S 0O  7  6
     A            SCYCL          6S 0H
     A            SDESC         17A  O  7 15
     A            SSTAT          1A  O  7 33
     A  31                                  COLOR(YLW)
     A            SCUR           7Y 2O  7 35EDTCDE(3)
     A            SSUG           7Y 2O  7 44EDTCDE(3)
     A                                      DSPATR(HI)
     A            SNEW           7Y 2B  7 53EDTCDE(4)
     A* The two dates are shown as text, set by the program: a title
     A* with no recorded price change carries 1900-01-01, which a
     A* MM/DD/YY date field cannot hold, and shows as 'none'.
     A            SDUE           8A  O  7 62
     A            SLSTC          8A  O  7 71
     A* Second line: the note - the bracket the price came from, or why
     A* the line is held. Blue, so it sits back behind the figures;
     A* yellow when held (status G), because G covers both a third-party
     A* approval and an override past the cap.
     A            SNOTE         60A  O  8 15
     A N31                                  COLOR(BLU)
     A  31                                  COLOR(YLW)
     A*
     A* Subfile control - title, selection, options and column headings
     A          R RPCCTL1                   SFLCTL(RPCSFL1)
     A                                      SFLSIZ(9999)
     A                                      SFLPAG(0006)
     A*                                     Load-all subfile: SFLSIZ is
     A*                                     larger than SFLPAG, so the
     A*                                     system does the paging.
     A*                                     Six to a page, two lines
     A*                                     each: rows 7 to 18.
     A                                      OVERLAY
     A  21                                  SFLDSP
     A  22                                  SFLDSPCTL
     A  23                                  SFLCLR
     A  24                                  SFLEND(*MORE)
     A            WDATE           L  O  1  2DATFMT(*MDY)
     A                                      DATSEP('/')
     A                                      COLOR(BLU)
     A                                  1 24'Work with Repricing Suggestions'
     A                                      DSPATR(HI)
     A                                  1 71'IVRRPCWRK'
     A                                      COLOR(BLU)
     A* Row 2 is a rule under the title: a blank field, underlined.
     A            WLINE1        78A  O  2  2DSPATR(UL)
     A                                      COLOR(BLU)
     A                                  3  2'Catalogue:'
     A            WDIVCAT        7S 0B  3 13
     A                                      DSPATR(HI)
     A                                  3 22'(0 = all)'
     A                                  3 40'Status:'
     A            WSTAT          1A  B  3 48
     A                                      DSPATR(HI)
     A                                  3 51'(blank = open)'
     A                                  4  2'Type option, press Enter.  2=Overr-
     A                                      ide  4=Reject  6=Approve'
     A                                      COLOR(PNK)
     A* Column headings: one constant, underlined end to end.
     A                                  6  2'Opt Item     Description       St -
     A                                      Current  Suggest      New Due      -
     A                                      Repriced'
     A                                      DSPATR(UL)
     A                                      DSPATR(HI)
     A*
     A* Footer - a rule, the keys and the message line. A record of its
     A* own, because a control record takes up every line from its first
     A* to its last, so lines below the subfile would overlap it.
     A* Written before each EXFMT of RPCCTL1.
     A          R RPCFTR1
     A                                      OVERLAY
     A            WLINE2        78A  O 22  2DSPATR(UL)
     A                                      COLOR(BLU)
     A                                 23  2'F3=Exit  F5=Refresh  F12=Cancel'
     A                                      COLOR(BLU)
     A                                 23 40'St: S=New A=Approved O=Override G=-
     A                                      Held'
     A                                      COLOR(BLU)
     A            WMSG          78A  O 24  2DSPATR(HI)
